<title>ARGENTINA: Argentine ports hit by general strike.</title>
<headline>Argentine ports hit by general strike.</headline>
<dateline>BUENOS AIRES 1996-12-26</dateline>
<text>
<p>Argentina's grain ports of Rosario and Quequen have been paralyzed by Thursday's 24-hour general strike, a national ports authority official said.</p>
<p>The port of Bahia Blanca is operating at 50 percent capacity, with 33 percent of personnel joining the strike, the official told Reuters.</p>
<p>He said he only had information from Terminal Four in the port of Buenos Aires, where 49 percent of workers were striking but scheduled operations had been carried out as planned.</p>
<p>The NABSA shipping agency said the other terminals in Buenos Aires appeared to be working normally.</p>
<p>((--Jason Webb, Buenos Aires Newsroom +541 318-0655))</p>
